                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1cf32579-758b-4340-b513-f38034584f0c",
                        "source_entry_id": "a6028767-3f0d-3d93-ad06-e31ab5cfa096",
                        "source_sense_description": "Prophétesse de l’antiquité",
                        "target_lang_word": "sibyl",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sibyl",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc4f9fe8-01bc-381e-b763-d4df9e30a09e",
                                        "entry_id": "f9c22f9b-b0af-3482-96ac-0896b5138269",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pagan female oracle or prophetess, especially the Cumaean sibyl."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59bf99e0-8aaf-45e7-9a99-2dcca52b54d3",
                                                "sense_id": "cc4f9fe8-01bc-381e-b763-d4df9e30a09e",
                                                "text": "A Sybill that had numbred in the world\nThe Sun to courſe, two hundred compaſſes,\nIn her Prophetticke furie ſow'd the Worke:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ab9dd5a-7982-42a6-b09b-8facff6a1859",
                                                "sense_id": "cc4f9fe8-01bc-381e-b763-d4df9e30a09e",
                                                "text": "\"Are you very anxious,\" asked he, \"to consult the sibyl?\" \"Nay,\" replied Francesea; \"I want faith.\" \"You will,\" replied he, \"nevertheless be amused with Madame de I'Hôpital's tact; she knows enough of the history of the individuals around to give a shrewd guess at the favourite fantasy of each, and that it will be successful is the summing up of her prophecy. She tells each what he wishes, and so obtains an easy belief.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bb533fd-2bd8-49f7-91b1-8844cfba4716",
                                                "sense_id": "cc4f9fe8-01bc-381e-b763-d4df9e30a09e",
                                                "text": "`Nay, wait, Kallikrates,' said Ayesha, who, standing with the lamp raised above her head, flooding with its light her own rich beauty and the cold wonder of the death-clothed form upon the bier, resembled an inspired Sibyl rather than a woman, as she rolled out her majestic sentences with a grandeur and a freedom of utterance which I am, alas! quite unable to reproduce."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d52adbcf-4335-4d66-866e-f21ccd58ad82",
                                                "sense_id": "cc4f9fe8-01bc-381e-b763-d4df9e30a09e",
                                                "text": "I used to read these tales in Homer when I was a lad. Then the Sibyl! I saw her at Cumae with my own eyes hanging in a jar; and when the boys cried to her, ‘Sibyl, what would you?' she'd answer, ‘I would die,'-- both of ‘em speaking Greek.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d4553b2f-39f3-4fde-939f-90b5bc5d5f3d",
                        "source_entry_id": "a6028767-3f0d-3d93-ad06-e31ab5cfa096",
